1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
A checkout that never finishes can trigger risky retries.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Two requests can hold different locks, then wait forever for each other.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Low CPU does not mean the service is healthy. Threads may be blocked.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Capture repeated thread dumps, inspect lock owners, and correlate JFR with traces.

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Keep transactions short. Avoid remote calls inside locks. Reconcile uncertain payments.

6
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Test contention, retries, and downstream failures before claiming improvement.
